/* Relayium — iOS app bundle, English (source of truth for the purpose strings).

   This file exists for the same reason the app bundle carries its own
   `CFBundleLocalizations`: the product's catalogs live in the RelayiumAppKit
   package bundle, and iOS never looks there for a purpose string. A system
   permission alert is drawn by the OS, from THIS bundle, before any Relayium
   code runs — so a sentence that is only in the package is a sentence the user
   never sees.

   `Info.plist` holds the same English text as the fallback. That duplication is
   deliberate and asserted: `IOSLocalNetworkPermissionTests` fails if the two
   drift, because the fallback is what a device with an unmatched language
   renders and it must not quietly become a different promise.

   Exactly one key, and it is the only protected resource this build declares.
   `NSCameraUsageDescription` is NOT here: the camera symbols the embedded
   WebRTC framework carries are an open upload blocker tracked in
   `docs/ios-app-store-submission.md`, and a purpose string for a feature the
   product does not have would be a false statement rather than a fix. */

/* Shown by iOS when a transfer first needs to reach the other device across
   this network. It describes the transfer — not discovery: the roster comes
   from Relayium's own server over ordinary internet access, and this app runs
   no Bonjour query and no subnet scan. */
"NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription" = "Relayium sends the files and messages you choose directly to the device you select, when that device is on the same network as this one.";
